  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The energy of an electromagnetic wave contained in a small volume oscillates with</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nepcK",
      "text": "Double the frequency of the wave",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "qUNlY",
      "text": "The frequency of the wave",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dpHfh",
      "text": "Half the frequency of the wave",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7VlTI",
      "text": "Zero frequency",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the energy confined within the electric component of an electromagnetic wave can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Let&#39;s assume that the equation of the electric component is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the expression for the electric field component from equation (2) into equation (1) and simplify to obtain the expression for the energy confined within the small volume&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#981;</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>From equation (3), it can be concluded that the frequency of oscillation of the energy confined within a small volume is double the frequency of the wave.</p></blockquote>",
